        "description": "The profile view writes user-supplied POST fields (address, phone, etc.) directly onto a User object and calls save(), which a scanner may flag as mass-assignment / broken object-level authorization (CWE-915/639). It is actually safe: the view is @login_required and mutates only request.user (the authenticated session owner, never an attacker-chosen id), and each attribute is assigned individually from a fixed whitelist of non-privileged fields (first_name, last_name, email, phone, address) - role, password, is_staff and other sensitive fields are never touched. There is no object lookup by client-supplied identifier, so no IDOR or privilege escalation is possible."
